00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:01.690
Sure.

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:11.280
You weren't kidding when you said "big."

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:14.350
When we're this close, 
all you can see are the fish,

00:07:14.350 --> 00:07:16.910
so it's like we're underwater 
with no one else around.

00:07:20.380 --> 00:07:23.880
Tamaru-kun, look! A whale shark! Wow!

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:27.800
They're bigger than I thought! And so cute!

00:07:31.510 --> 00:07:34.380
What a great smile, Ichika-chan!

00:07:34.380 --> 00:07:36.370
Please don't take pictures without warning.

00:07:36.370 --> 00:07:40.140
Sorry about that. You just looked 
so cute, all excited and stuff.

00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:44.180
Masuda-san, do you have Rio's contact info?

00:07:44.180 --> 00:07:45.570
Hm? Yeah, I do.

00:07:45.570 --> 00:07:48.600
My phone died, so I haven't been 
able to get a hold of her.

00:07:48.600 --> 00:07:51.650
You can use my phone. 
Go ahead and contact her.

00:07:51.650 --> 00:07:53.230
Thank you.

00:07:53.230 --> 00:07:56.070
Arima, you know him?

00:07:56.070 --> 00:07:59.160
Masuda-san is Ryo-san's friend. 
I just met him recently.

00:07:59.380 --> 00:08:04.360
Ah, so you know Ryo, eh? 
Nice to meet you, my boy.

00:08:04.360 --> 00:08:06.890
I'm not your boy. My name's Tamaru.

00:08:06.890 --> 00:08:08.920
<i>Of course he had to know that guy.</i>

00:08:09.310 --> 00:08:10.880
Hello, Rio?

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:13.220
I just borrowed Masuda-san's cellphone.

00:08:11.910 --> 00:08:14.650
Hey, did I get in your way?

00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:19.620
Yeah. Okay, we can meet up later. 
Okay. Let's meet at the aquarium.

00:08:14.650 --> 00:08:17.860
Wha— It's not like that.

00:08:17.860 --> 00:08:18.810
You sure?

00:08:19.620 --> 00:08:25.080
<i>Ryo seemed really worried about 
Ichika-chan. I guess he might be why.</i>

00:08:25.790 --> 00:08:28.150
I bought some gifts! Aren't they cute?

00:08:28.370 --> 00:08:30.240
Wow, they are!

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:32.750
Want to make plans for 
our free time tomorrow?

00:08:32.750 --> 00:08:33.820
Sure.

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:39.910
What's wrong? Someone calling you?

00:08:39.910 --> 00:08:41.470
Uh, yeah...

00:08:41.470 --> 00:08:42.790
You don't need to answer?

00:08:43.930 --> 00:08:44.670
Figured
it out

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:46.620
Why don't you take it in the hallway?

00:08:46.620 --> 00:08:49.050
Y-Yeah, I will.

00:08:55.380 --> 00:08:58.260
You know that I'm on my school 
trip right now, don't you?

00:08:58.470 --> 00:09:01.850
I'm terribly sorry. There's just something 
that I absolutely had to confirm.

00:09:02.070 --> 00:09:03.190
<i>Confirm?</i>

00:09:03.190 --> 00:09:07.770
I called Masuda a moment ago because 
I needed to talk to him, and he said...

00:09:07.920 --> 00:09:13.490
<b>Jasmine
Tea</b>

00:09:08.450 --> 00:09:13.890
Actually, I'm in Okinawa with Ichika-chan and 
her class as a photographer on their school trip!

00:09:13.890 --> 00:09:20.400
And, yeah... Knowing him, it could be a joke, 
so I wanted to confirm with you.

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:23.160
<i>Um... Yes, Masuda-san is here.</i>

00:09:24.620 --> 00:09:26.960
That asshole... I'm so jealous!

00:09:24.810 --> 00:09:32.250
<b>Grrr</b>

00:09:28.010 --> 00:09:29.870
<i>I mean, he's working...</i>

00:09:29.870 --> 00:09:32.250
I know, but... Damn it!

00:09:32.640 --> 00:09:35.190
<i>More importantly, how's your trip going?</i>

00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:39.650
It's a lot of fun. 
I went to the aquarium today.

00:09:39.650 --> 00:09:41.630
The whale shark was really cute.

00:09:41.630 --> 00:09:45.100
<i>Ah, a whale shark. I don't 
think I've seen one before.</i>

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:47.040
<i>Are you feeling okay, by the way?</i>

00:09:47.040 --> 00:09:50.770
Jeez, you worry too much. 
You're not my mom.

00:09:52.150 --> 00:09:53.900
<i>Am I acting like Yuriko-san?</i>

00:09:53.900 --> 00:09:56.600
Could you not address my mother by her name?

00:09:56.600 --> 00:10:02.160
Also, if you wanted to know if Masuda-san 
was here, why didn't you just call Rio?

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:05.720
Well, if I'm going to call one of you, 
I'd prefer to call you.

00:10:05.720 --> 00:10:07.540
And if my instincts are correct,

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:10.040
I'm pretty sure you're starting 
to miss hearing my vo—

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:11.040
I absolutely am not.

00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:12.790
You must be missing m—

00:10:12.790 --> 00:10:15.090
That is the last thing you need to worry about.

00:10:15.870 --> 00:10:17.690
<i>I'm sorry. I'm only kidding.</i>

00:10:18.980 --> 00:10:22.170
I did call about Masuda,

00:10:23.150 --> 00:10:27.330
but the biggest reason I'm calling you 
is that I wanted to hear your voice.

00:10:32.070 --> 00:10:34.900
Having Rio and Masuda-san here

00:10:35.690 --> 00:10:38.030
while you're not here...

00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:40.160
does make me miss you...

00:10:41.770 --> 00:10:43.430
a little.

00:10:45.480 --> 00:10:46.480
